WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.851
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.151 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:15.460
Unit twenty-three: Prepositions of Place. Today you will say exactly where things are.

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.134
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.368
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:24.229
Next to.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:27.472
Next to means at the side of something.

8
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.793
The bank is next to the shop.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:33.268
Your turn. Say: Next to.

10
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.274
Next to.

11
00:00:38.017 --> 00:00:38.762
Between.

12
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.831
Between means in the middle of two things.

13
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.254
The cat is between the chairs.

14
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.247
Your turn. Say: Between.

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:50.706
Between.

16
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.265
Behind.

17
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.238
Behind means at the back of something.

18
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.455
The ball is behind the door.

19
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.435
Your turn. Say: Behind.

20
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.289
Behind.

21
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.074
In front of.

22
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:09.257
In front of means at the front of something.

23
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.583
The bus is in front of the school.

24
00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:14.754
Your turn. Say: In front of.

25
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.508
In front of.

26
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.019
Under.

27
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:22.842
Under means below something.

28
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.974
The cat is under the table.

29
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:27.969
Your turn. Say: Under.

30
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:31.683
Under.

31
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.370
Opposite.

32
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:37.149
Opposite means on the other side facing something.

33
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.715
The school is opposite the park.

34
00:01:40.317 --> 00:01:43.248
Your turn. Say: Opposite.

35
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.055
Opposite.

36
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:48.597
Near.

37
00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:51.374
Near means close to something.

38
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:53.484
I live near the market.

39
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:56.353
Your turn. Say: Near.

40
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.271
Near.

41
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:01.878
Above.

42
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:04.999
Above means higher than something.

43
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.235
The clock is above the door.

44
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.991
Your turn. Say: Above.

45
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:13.695
Above.

46
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.325
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:22.962
Visal, where is your school? Can you describe it with a place word?

48
00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:33.032
My school is next to a park and opposite a market. These words are prepositions of place. They tell us exactly where something is.

49
00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:35.849
Can you give more examples?

50
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:47.003
The cat is under the table. The clock is above the door. The bank is between the shop and the school. The bus is in front of the gate and the dog is behind it.

51
00:02:48.117 --> 00:02:49.838
Where do we put the preposition?

52
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:59.674
After the verb be and before the noun: The book is under the chair. We can also use there is: There is a tree behind the house.

53
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.531
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:06.393
Grammar focus: Prepositions of place.

55
00:03:06.693 --> 00:03:07.833
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.236
The cat is under the table.

57
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.347
The bank is between the shop and the school.

58
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.936
The clock is above the door.

59
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:22.998
Use next to, between, behind, in front of, under, opposite, near and above after be to say exactly where something is.

60
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.180
Be careful! Don't say: The bank is in front the school.

61
00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:32.085
Say: The bank is in front of the school.

62
00:03:32.385 --> 00:03:33.862
Say in front of.

63
00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.377
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.412
Finding Places.

65
00:03:39.712 --> 00:03:42.547
My school is next to a park and opposite a market.

66
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:46.647
The bank is between the shop and the post office.

67
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:50.724
There is a bus in front of the gate, and a tree behind the building.

68
00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:54.940
The clock is above the door, and my bag is under my desk.

69
00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:57.944
I live near the school, so I walk.

70
00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:03.256
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:04.117 --> 00:04:06.467
The cat is blank the table. (below)

72
00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.699
A, under. B, above. C, between.

73
00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:16.105
The answer is A: under.

74
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.693
The clock is blank the door. (higher)

75
00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:23.333
A, under. B, behind. C, above.

76
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:28.947
The answer is C: above.

77
00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:33.223
The shop is blank the bank and the school. (in the middle)

78
00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:36.794
A, between. B, opposite. C, near.

79
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:42.809
The answer is A: between.

80
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.520
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:52.109
A, The park is in front the school.. B, The park is in front of the school.. C, The park is front of the school..

82
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:58.850
The answer is B: The park is in front of the school..

83
00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:02.399
According to the reading, where is the bank?

84
00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:08.663
A, between the shop and the post office. B, under the table. C, near the clock.

85
00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.674
The answer is A: between the shop and the post office.

86
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:20.007
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.735
Where is your school? Use two prepositions.

88
00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.120
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:48.035
My school is next to a small park and opposite a big market. It is near my house, so I walk there every day. I use next to, opposite and near to say exactly where my school is.

90
00:05:48.335 --> 00:05:49.974
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:54.975
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and prepositions of place.

92
00:05:55.275 --> 00:05:58.938
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:05:59.238 --> 00:06:01.971
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:02.271 --> 00:06:04.958
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

